@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB Customer Contact Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki contact integration to OSB works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Kchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneiki - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| bso.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| bso.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create customer contacts
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts on Koroneiki that later get sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki2                       |

Scenario: Create customer contacts executed by agent
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts executed by agent on Koroneiki that later get sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki User" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User   |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1   |
	| Update Date                 | Today            |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A              |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member           |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User                       |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki User" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User   |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2   |
	| Update Date                 | Today            |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A              |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member           |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User                       |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki2                       |

Scenario: Create customer contacts with middle names
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts with middle names on Koroneiki that later get sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	| Middle Name   | User                                 |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	| Middle Name   | User                                 |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB User Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB User Koroneiki1                  |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB User Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB User Koroneiki2                  |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB User Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB User Koroneiki1           |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB User Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB User Koroneiki1                  |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB User Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB User Koroneiki2           |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB User Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB User Koroneiki2                  |

Scenario: Create customer contacts on account with special characters
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts on Koroneiki account with special characters that later get sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                          | |
	| Description           | 100% $$$$$ making & awesome org for our @customers! ^_^ v +-= | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                                                  | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}                                 | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                                                  | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                          | |
	| Region                | United States                                                 | |
	| Status                | Active                                                        | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                                            | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com                                  | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer" and "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Updated Team" and "Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member" and "OSB Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer        |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                         |
	| Update Description          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} Member |
	| Update Date                 | Today                                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Koroneiki2                       |

Scenario: Create customer contacts via nested fields before creation
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts via nested fields before creation on Koroneiki that later get sent to OSB

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent customer contact with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I rename the first contact nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for a nonexistent customer contact with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I rename the second contact nested field variable
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                                                | |
	| Contact Nested Field  | ${staticContactsNestedField1},${staticContactsNestedField2} | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                        | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki                               | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                                                | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}                               | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                                                | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                        | |
	| Region                | United States                                               | |
	| Status                | Active                                                      | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                                          | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com                                | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
